%N A398595 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * H(2*k) * H(2*k,2)/k, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number, and H(k,2) = A007406(k)/A007407(k) is the k-th harmonic number of order 2.
%H A398595 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.53, pp. 450-451, eq. (4.181), section 5.53, p. 468, section 6.53, pp. 770-779.
%H A398595 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398595 Equals log(2)*Pi*G/4 - 137*zeta(4)/128 + 35*log(2)*zeta(3)/64 - 3*log(2)^2*zeta(2)/8 + 5*log(2)^4/96 + Pi*Im(Li_3((1+i)/2))/2 + 5*Li_4(1/2)/4, where G is Catalan's constant (A006752), and i is the imaginary unit.
%e A398595 1.0538613468754433917731990730805244992974634891917402...
%t A398595 RealDigits[Log[2]*Pi*Catalan/4 - 137*Zeta[4]/128 + 35*Log[2]*Zeta[3]/64 - 3*Log[2]^2*Zeta[2]/8 + 5*Log[2]^4/96 + Pi*Im[PolyLog[3, (1 + I)/2]]/2 + 5*PolyLog[4, 1/2]/4, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A398595 (PARI) log(2)*Pi*Catalan/4 - 137*zeta(4)/128 + 35*log(2)*zeta(3)/64 - 3*log(2)^2*zeta(2)/8 + 5*log(2)^4/96 + Pi*imag(polylog(3, (1+I)/2))/2 + 5*polylog(4, 1/2)/4
